  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `design.md` §5 (access model), §4 (membership sync), §8.4 (ACS reconcile), and spec Unresolved Questions to fix the exact decision boundary (private-grant only; open stays ADR-034).</step>
    <step order="2">Grep + read the `GrantAccess`/POA precedent (`PlaybookSharingService`) — how it shares, revokes, and how a BFF read honours the shared access.</step>
    <step order="3">Grep + read the overlay precedent (`GrantExternalAccessEndpoint` + `sprk_externalrecordaccess`) — how grants are recorded and how the BFF query-filter reads them.</step>
    <step order="4">Read the ADR-034 `MembershipResolverService` derivation to determine how each private-grant option composes with open membership at BFF read time.</step>
    <step order="5">Build a comparison matrix across: enforcement correctness in the BFF filter (042/050), composition with ADR-034, revocation + point-forward (D-04), auditability, ACS-reconcile compatibility (041), internal-now/external-later reach.</step>
    <step order="6">Make the decision. If the options materially diverge on correctness/safety, raise a 🔔 Human Input Required escalation (root §6) with the recommendation; otherwise record the pick.</step>
    <step order="7">Write `notes/spikes/002-private-grant-decision.md`: decision, rationale (matrix), rejected alternative, and a "consumed by 042/041/050" section specifying exactly how the enforcement filter + reconcile job must use the chosen mechanism.</step>
    <step order="8">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (002 ✅) + `current-task.md`; confirm task 042 is unblocked (or the escalation is pending).</step>
  </steps>

